<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Albania</h1><p class="st-meta">1991 CE – present · capital Tirana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Present-day Albania, a parliamentary republic since the end of communism in 1991 and a NATO member seeking to join the European Union.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mass protests and emigration in 1990 forced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peoples-socialist-republic-of-albania">People's Socialist Republic of Albania</a> to permit opposition parties. After the first multi-party elections, the country was renamed the Republic of Albania in April 1991. In 1992 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-of-albania">Democratic Party</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sali-berisha">Sali Berisha</a> won power, ending communist rule.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Albania is a parliamentary republic with a president elected by parliament. Religion returned to public life after decades of state atheism, and private enterprise and emigration transformed society. The collapse of pyramid investment schemes in 1997 caused near-anarchy and an international intervention. In 1999 Albania sheltered hundreds of thousands of refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>. Politics has been dominated by the rivalry of the Democratic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialist-party-of-albania">Socialist</a> parties.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Albania joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 2009, became an EU candidate in 2014 and opened accession negotiations in 2022. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edi-rama">Edi Rama's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialist-party-of-albania">Socialists</a> have governed since 2013, and tourism has become a major industry.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/albania.jpg" alt="Albania" width="320" height="229"><figcaption>Image: Sadik Kaceli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1991 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tirana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sali Berisha, Fatos Nano, Edi Rama</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Albania</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Albania</dd></dl></aside></div>
